    {
      "id": "PpQk5f",
      "title": "Oyakodon",
      "content": "## Ingredients (1 serving)\n- 100 g chicken thigh\n- 2 eggs\n- 1/4 onion\n- 1 bowl of rice\n- 80 ml dashi; 1 tbsp each soy sauce and mirin; 1 tsp sugar\n\n## Method\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    A[\"Cut chicken and onion\"] --> B[\"Simmer in sauce\"] --> C[\"Add beaten eggs\"] --> D((\"Serve over rice\"))\n```\n\n> The child nodes “Chicken” and “Egg” are the same nodes found under Ingredients.",
      "sortMode": "manual",
      "sortDirection": "asc"
    },
    {
      "id": "6VeRkF",
      "title": "Nikujaga",
      "content": "## Ingredients (2 servings)\n- 2 potatoes\n- 100 g thinly sliced beef\n- 1/2 onion and 1/2 carrot\n- 200 ml dashi; 2 tbsp each soy sauce and mirin; 1 tbsp sugar\n\n## Method\n1. Cut the vegetables into bite-sized pieces.\n2. Stir-fry the beef and vegetables, then add the dashi and seasonings.\n3. Cover with a drop lid and simmer for 15 minutes.",
      "sortMode": "manual",
      "sortDirection": "asc"
    },
    {
      "id": "zAXEvM",
      "title": "Omelette",
      "content": "## Ingredients (1 serving)\n- 3 eggs\n- 1 tbsp milk\n- 10 g butter; salt and pepper to taste\n\n## Method\n1. Mix the eggs, milk, salt, and pepper.\n2. Pour into a pan with melted butter and stir in broad strokes.\n3. While still soft, fold toward the edge and shape.",
      "sortMode": "manual",
      "sortDirection": "asc"
    },
    {
      "id": "dE4McW",
      "title": "Chicken sauté",
      "content": "## Ingredients (1 serving)\n- 1 chicken thigh\n- Salt and pepper to taste; 1 tsp olive oil\n\n## Method\n1. Season the chicken with salt and pepper.\n2. Cook skin-side down over medium heat, then turn when the skin is crisp.\n3. Cover and cook through.",
      "sortMode": "manual",
      "sortDirection": "asc"
    },
    {
      "id": "XuVohB",
      "title": "Potato salad",
      "content": "## Ingredients (2 servings)\n- 2 potatoes\n- 1 boiled egg\n- 1/2 cucumber\n- 3 tbsp mayonnaise; salt and pepper to taste\n\n## Method\n1. Boil and mash the potatoes.\n2. Combine with the chopped boiled egg and cucumber.\n3. Mix with mayonnaise, salt, and pepper.",
      "sortMode": "manual",
      "sortDirection": "asc"
    },
